h2kvm for Debian
====================

Configuration
-------------

The system-wide configuration file is located at:
  /etc/h2kvm/config.yaml

This file is marked as a conffile and will be preserved during package upgrades.

Edit this file to:
- Add allowed directories for VM image access
- Configure conversion cache settings
- Set default libvirt parameters
- Enable daemon mode (future feature)

Container Isolation
-------------------

By default, LVM operations (such as volume group activation and logical volume
scanning) run inside a Podman or Docker container to isolate the host from
potentially dangerous disk metadata. This prevents rogue LVM labels on migrated
disks from interfering with the host's own volume groups.

To use container isolation, install podman or docker.io:
  $ sudo apt install podman
  or
  $ sudo apt install docker.io

Container isolation can be disabled per-run with the CLI flag:
  $ h2kvm local --no-container-isolation ...

Or permanently in the system configuration file:
  /etc/h2kvm/config.yaml

Set:
  container_isolation: false

Migration Templates
-------------------

Example migration configurations are provided in:
  /etc/h2kvm/migrations/

Copy and customize these templates for your VMs:
  $ sudo cp /etc/h2kvm/migrations/photon-example.yaml \
            /etc/h2kvm/migrations/my-vm.yaml
  $ sudo vi /etc/h2kvm/migrations/my-vm.yaml
  $ sudo h2kvmctl --config /etc/h2kvm/migrations/my-vm.yaml

System User
-----------

The package automatically creates a system user 'h2kvm' for daemon mode
operation. This user is added to the following groups (if they exist):
- qemu
- kvm
- libvirt
- disk

Directories
-----------

The following directories are created and owned by the h2kvm user:
- /var/lib/h2kvm - Main data directory
- /var/lib/h2kvm/conversions - Conversion cache
- /var/log/h2kvm - Log files

Systemd Services
----------------

The package provides systemd service units:
- h2kvm.service - Main daemon service
- h2kvm@.service - Template service for multiple instances

To enable and start the service:
  $ sudo systemctl enable --now h2kvm.service

Documentation
-------------

Full documentation is available in:
  /usr/share/doc/h2kvm/

Man pages:
  $ man h2kvm
  $ man h2kvm-local
  $ man h2kvm-vsphere
  $ man h2kvm-hyperv
  $ man h2kvm-azure
  $ man h2kvm.conf

